ions. DRF dispatch performs authentication and permission checks before calling the action handler, so an unauthenticated request is short-circuited before download/file_response returns a file.","evidenceIds":["ev-e379811e1360266f7ca6","ev-1b42f0a7ffddbc8171a6"]},{"id":"q1-b2","condition":"The requester is authenticated but fails the DocumentViewSet/PaperlessObjectPermissions request-level checks applicable to GET.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"The view set applies PaperlessObjectPermissions to the download action unless the action overrides it; the shown download declaration does not override permission_classes. DRF runs those permission checks before entering download. The exact effective model-permission result depends on the authenticated user's deployed permissions/backends.","evidenceIds":["ev-e379811e1360266f7ca6","ev-92b8b3c7319612762e61","ev-1b42f0a7ffddbc8171a6"]},{"id":"q1-b3","condition":"The request passes upstream authentication/model-permission checks, and no version query parameter is supplied while the addressed pk is a root document.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The version resolver defines the effective document as the newest version for a root, falling back to the root itself if no version exists. The download handler delegates to file_response, but the returned source does not include file_response's body, so the final linkage from this resolver to the downloaded path is a precise source gap rather than a proven call chain.","evidenceIds":["ev-92b8b3c7319612762e61","ev-2a1d3ddc4932ff33a170","ev-bafdf376f4f14ecef463"]},{"id":"q1-b4","condition":"The request passes upstream checks, no version query parameter is supplied, and the addressed pk is itself a historical version row.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"resolve_effective_document preserves the addressed version row when the request row has a root_document_id and no explicit version parameter. Thus the versioning helper would select that version rather than automatically replacing it with the latest. Whether download/file_response uses this exact helper is not proven by the returned file_response source.","evidenceIds":["ev-2a1d3ddc4932ff33a170","ev-92b8b3c7319612762e61"]},{"id":"q1-b5","condition":"A syntactically valid version=<id> is supplied and that id is either the root itself or a version whose root_document_id equals the requested root id.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The resolver accepts only the root or a member of that root's version family and returns the selected candidate. This can change which Document row supplies file metadata/path and therefore which version's original/archive representation would be returned, if file_response uses the resolver as the nearby retrieve path does. The evidence does not establish that authorization is re-bound to that selected candidate.","evidenceIds":["ev-2a1d3ddc4932ff33a170","ev-bafdf376f4f14ecef463"]},{"id":"q1-b6","condition":"version is non-integer, names a nonexistent document, or names a document outside the requested root/version family.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"The version resolver reports INVALID for a non-integer and NOT_FOUND for nonexistent or unrelated candidates. The download action converts Document.DoesNotExist and FileNotFoundError to HTTP 404, but the returned source omits the adapter that maps VersionResolutionError in file_response/_resolve_file_doc, so the exact HTTP response for each version-resolution error is not fully established here. No unrelated document is accepted as the selected version by the resolver.","evidenceIds":["ev-2a1d3ddc4932ff33a170","ev-92b8b3c7319612762e61"]},{"id":"q1-b7","condition":"The selected effective document has an archive representation and the request chooses the archive/default representation rather than original.","disposition":"conditional","explanation":"The returned source establishes that Document representations distinguish source_path from archive_path and that archive selection is