lse, and the user or one of the user's groups has the required object grant.","disposition":"allow","explanation":"The owner-aware rule permits when Guardian's ObjectPermissionChecker reports the requested permission on the object. The actual user/group grants are unspecified, so this branch cannot be selected for the scenario.","evidenceIds":["ev-ca93c4b7a33584c06bfa"]},{"id":"q1-b12","condition":"The download path applies the owner-aware check, the object is owned by someone else, and no applicable object grant exists.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"None of the owner-aware allow alternatives would hold. The actual ownership/grant state is unspecified, and the unread file_response body prevents proving which document row is supplied to this check.","evidenceIds":["ev-ca93c4b7a33584c06bfa"]},{"id":"q1-b13","condition":"A different valid version in the same root/version family is selected.","disposition":"unknown","explanation":"Selection clearly changes the effective Document candidate within the family and can therefore change the physical original/archive file returned. The returned evidence does not prove that it changes the authorization resource: the candidate lookup itself does not perform an owner/object-grant check, while the decisive file_response authorization binding is in the unread source range. Accordingly, do not assume either per-version authorization or root-level authorization.","evidenceIds":["ev-2a1d3ddc4932ff33a170","ev-bafdf376f4f14ecef463"]},{"id":"q1-b14","condition":"The selected concrete file path does not exist, or the addressed Document lookup fails in the delegated response path.","disposition":"deny","explanation":"download catches FileNotFoundError and Document.DoesNotExist from file_response and raises Http404, so no file is returned in those branches.","evidenceIds":["ev-92b8b3c7319612762e61"]},{"id":"q1-b15","condition":"All applicable authentication, model-permission, object-authorization, version-family, representation, and 